title: no validation of status, priority, class or due on any write path
updated: 2026-08-10T01:40:24Z
---

Found independently by two audit lanes. `status`, `priority`, `class` and `due`
are never validated on any write path. All of these exit 0 and write an invalid
board:

    karr move 1 totally-invalid      # rc=0  "Moved task 1: backlog -> totally-invalid"
    karr create "x" --status bogus   # rc=0
    karr create "x" --priority bogus # rc=0
    karr create "x" --class bogus    # rc=0
    karr create "x" --due not-a-date # rc=0
    karr edit 1 --status bogus       # rc=0
    karr pick --claim a --move bogus # rc=0, moves the task to "bogus"

The board then breaks in place: `karr move 1 --next` -> `Unknown status:
totally-invalid` (rc=1) and the task sits in no column, invisible on `karr board`
but counted in the total. `karr list` column alignment breaks too.

kanban-md validates all of these in `internal/task/validate.go`
(`ValidateStatus`/`ValidatePriority`/`ValidateClass`), called from `cmd/move.go:169`,
`cmd/create.go:211,217,223`, `cmd/edit.go:287,294,325`, `cmd/handoff.go:107`,
`cmd/pick.go:61,66`.

Expected per ADR 0002: reject with **exit 2** (invalid option value). Note this
is not on the CLAUDE.md roadmap the way WIP limits and dependency checking are —
it is a plain gap.

Related: `karr edit` cannot clear a `due` date at all once set.
Fixed and merged into main (3dac607); full suite green at 93 files / 630 tests.
Reproduced before the fix, regression test verified to fail against the pre-fix
code. Note the #68 trigger change: started is now stamped on the first move out
of the FIRST CONFIGURED status, per kanban-md lifecycle.go, not out of the
literal in-progress.
